Subject: CK: FMHA attention-sink fixes

Three fixes on the sink path. TransformerEngine reaches all of them through
softmax_offset (softmax_type != "vanilla"), which sets has_sink with
sink_size = 0.

fmha_bwd_kernel.hpp: sink_ptr was indexed as a [batch, nhead] buffer. It holds
one value per head, as the fwd kernels already assume. Corrupted
d_softmax_offset and the q/k/v gradients for every batch index > 0.

block_fmha_pipeline_qr_ks_vs.hpp, block_fmha_pipeline_qr_ks_vs_async.hpp: the
bias, randval and K/V windows are built at kv_load_start, which already equals
seqlen_k_start when no sink prefix exists, but each kHasSink block moved them a
second time by (seqlen_k_start - sink_seq_end) on iteration 0. Guarding on an
actual sink phase makes the move inert when num_sink_loop == 0. This broke sink
combined with a local (sliding-window) mask: in QRKSVS the K/V check is live, so
forward output was garbage (rel. err ~1.0) for bias + SWA + sink. The bias and
randval windows are wrong in both pipelines.

fmha_fwd_kernel.hpp: the sink logit was divided by kargs.scale_s while the
softmax variant uses scale_s * q_descale * k_descale under PERTENSOR, so the
round trip left the logit scaled by q_descale * k_descale. Both now go through
GetSoftmaxScale(). Affects fp8 per-tensor quantization only; with NO_SCALE the
helper returns kargs.scale_s and the generated code is unchanged.

Source: rocm-libraries branch knasyrov/mha_sink_fix, commits 4727153c27 and
5c5ba106fd, plus the bwd index fix.

